## kix

Kubernetes manifest generator

Usage: kix [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  build        Render manifests to stdout
  diff         Compare the build with the live cluster or a directory, read-only
  plan         Preview a deploy as a server-side dry run
  check        Evaluate a cluster and report build-time checks and scorecard findings
  deploy       Wave-based deployment with confirmation
  status       Resource health table
  list         List clusters, packages, or other resources
  graph        Dependency DAG visualization
  bundle       Package a built cluster into a standalone `.kixbundle` file
  inspect      Summarize a cluster's rendered resources by namespace and kind
  gc           Garbage-collect stale Kix-managed resources
  migrate      One-off cluster migrations
  rollback     Rollback to the previous activation
  export       Export cluster manifests as plain Kubernetes YAML (exit-strategy / audit bundle)
  logs         Tail logs for a package's primary workload
  pf           Port-forward to a package's primary workload
  health       Cluster integrity walk: dependency-presence check via identity-hashes
  drift        Content drift check via applied-hash stamps (cluster-only, no build)
  snapshot     Manage cluster snapshots for CI/offline use
  images       List all container images in a cluster activation (for airgap preloading)
  completions  Generate shell completions
  doctor       Check the Kix installation
  compliance   Compliance exports: SBOM, SLSA attestations, audit bundles
  pin          Resolve image references and record them in a committed pin file
  lib          Manage the Kix library this project pins in flake.lock
  self         Install, list, and remove versions of Kix
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format (text, json, yaml, markdown). Default varies by command

          Possible values:
          - text
          - json
          - yaml
          - markdown: GitHub-flavored markdown suitable for PR comments
          
          [env: KIX_OUTPUT]

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (-v, -vv, etc.)
          
          [env: KIX_VERBOSE]

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output
          
          [env: KIX_QUIET]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (also respects NO_COLOR env per no-color.org spec)

      --context <CONTEXT>
          Kubeconfig context to use
          
          [env: KIX_CONTEXT]

      --flake <FLAKE>
          Flake reference to evaluate clusters from (default: current directory)
          
          [env: KIX_FLAKE]
          [default: .]

      --no-cache
          Skip the SQLite eval cache (always re-evaluate from Nix)
          
          [env: KIX_NO_CACHE]

      --override-input <INPUT> <URL>
          Override a flake input's URL (repeatable: `--override-input INPUT URL`).
          
          Forwards `--override-input` to every `nix` subprocess. When this flag is not set, Kix reads space-separated `INPUT URL` pairs from `KIX_OVERRIDE_INPUT`.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Plugins: `kix NAME ARGS...` runs `kix-NAME ARGS...` from PATH.

