## kix bundle

Package a built cluster into a standalone `.kixbundle` file

A bundle (`.kixbundle`) is a seekable zstd archive containing every store file in the build and its references, allowing `kix plan`, `kix deploy`, and `kix graph` to run with `--bundle` on machines without Nix. Readers recompute every store path from its content and references and reject any mismatch.

Usage: kix bundle [OPTIONS] <CLUSTER> [FILE]

Arguments:
  <CLUSTER>
          Cluster name

  [FILE]
          Output path for the bundle [default: <CLUSTER>.kixbundle]

Options:
  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (-v, -vv, etc.)
          
          [env: KIX_VERBOSE]

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output
          
          [env: KIX_QUIET]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (also respects NO_COLOR env per no-color.org spec)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

