          Disable colored output (also respects NO_COLOR env per no-color.org spec)

      --flake <FLAKE>
          Flake reference to evaluate clusters from (default: current directory)
          
          [env: KIX_FLAKE]
          [default: .]

      --no-cache
          Skip the SQLite eval cache (always re-evaluate from Nix)
          
          [env: KIX_NO_CACHE]

      --override-input <INPUT> <URL>
          Override a flake input's URL (repeatable: `--override-input INPUT URL`).
          
          Forwards `--override-input` to every `nix` subprocess. When this flag is not set, Kix reads space-separated `INPUT URL` pairs from `KIX_OVERRIDE_INPUT`.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

## kix gc

Garbage-collect stale Kix-managed resources

Usage: kix gc [OPTIONS] <CLUSTER>

Arguments:
  <CLUSTER>
          Cluster name

Options:
  -y, --yes
          Skip confirmation prompt

      --hard
          Full cluster scan (default: diff old vs new activation store graphs)

      --operator
          Delegate garbage collection to the operator (deletes the Activation records the retention policy retires)

      --include-unstamped
          Also delete resources that carry the Kix label but no `kix.run/identity-hash`. Kix never applied those, so by default `--hard` only reports them

      --include-unattributed
          With `--hard`, also evaluate Kix resources that reference no Activation record on the cluster. When multiple Kix clusters share a Kubernetes cluster, Kix cannot tell which cluster owns unattributed resources, so by default `--hard` only reports them

      --include-copies
          With `--hard`, also check copies against the build. A copy carries Kix's labels and annotations, but Kix never wrote it: another program, usually an operator, copied them from an object Kix made. By default `--hard` only lists copies

      --keep <N>
          Minimum number of newest completed (`Superseded`) Activation records to retain as rollback targets, regardless of age (`0` retains none)
          
          [default: 10]

      --keep-max <N>
          Maximum number of `Superseded` Activation records to retain, bounding the size of the `kix.run/activations` annotation on managed resources
          
          [default: 50]

      --keep-for <DURATION>
          Beyond `--keep`, retire records older than this duration (`30d`, `12h`, `45m`, or a bare number of days; `0` or `off` disables age-based retirement)
          
          [default: 30d]

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (-v, -vv, etc.)
          
          [env: KIX_VERBOSE]

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output
          
          [env: KIX_QUIET]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (also respects NO_COLOR env per no-color.org spec)

      --context <CONTEXT>
          Kubeconfig context to use
          
          [env: KIX_CONTEXT]

      --flake <FLAKE>
          Flake reference to evaluate clusters from (default: current directory)
          
          [env: KIX_FLAKE]
          [default: .]

      --override-input <INPUT> <URL>
          Override a flake input's URL (repeatable: `--override-input INPUT URL`).
          
          Forwards `--override-input` to every `nix` subprocess. When this flag is not set, Kix reads space-separated `INPUT URL` pairs from `KIX_OVERRIDE_INPUT`.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

