## kix migrate domain

Migrate this cluster's Kix records from a retired API group to `kix.run`.

Copies every Activation record to the current API group with its status history intact, verifies each copy by name and phase, removes the operator finalizer from the old records, and deletes the old CRDs. PackageInstance records are not copied because the next deploy recreates them from the build.

If the Kix operator runs on this cluster, scale it to 0 before running this command. An older operator watching the retired API group will re-add its finalizer and delete active resources when the old CRDs are removed. Before copying or deleting anything, this command clears the old finalizers, waits briefly, and aborts if an operator re-adds them.

Safe to rerun if interrupted: existing copies are skipped and missing status subresources are repaired. After migration completes, upgrade the operator image, scale it back up, and deploy.

Usage: kix migrate domain [OPTIONS] <CLUSTER>

Arguments:
  <CLUSTER>
          Cluster name

Options:
      --dry-run
          Print the plan and stop

  -y, --yes
          Skip the confirmation prompt

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (-v, -vv, etc.)
          
          [env: KIX_VERBOSE]

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output
          
          [env: KIX_QUIET]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (also respects NO_COLOR env per no-color.org spec)

      --context <CONTEXT>
          Kubeconfig context to use
          
          [env: KIX_CONTEXT]

      --flake <FLAKE>
          Flake reference to evaluate clusters from (default: current directory)
          
          [env: KIX_FLAKE]
          [default: .]

      --override-input <INPUT> <URL>
          Override a flake input's URL (repeatable: `--override-input INPUT URL`).
          
          Forwards `--override-input` to every `nix` subprocess. When this flag is not set, Kix reads space-separated `INPUT URL` pairs from `KIX_OVERRIDE_INPUT`.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

