## kix export

Export cluster manifests as plain Kubernetes YAML (exit-strategy / audit bundle)

Usage: kix export [OPTIONS] <CLUSTER>

Arguments:
  <CLUSTER>
          Cluster name

Options:
      --out <OUT>
          Output directory (nested: `<out>/<namespace>/<Kind>-<name>.yaml`)
          
          [default: ./kix-export]

      --for <MODE>
          Export mode: `exit` strips `kix.run/*` annotations and omits Kix-internal CRs (`Activation`, `PackageInstance`) for a clean handoff; `audit` preserves all metadata for compliance evidence

          Possible values:
          - exit:  Plain Kubernetes YAML without Kix metadata, suitable for `kubectl apply`, Flux, or Argo
          - audit: Preserve `kix.run/*` provenance annotations for audit evidence
          
          [default: exit]

      --force
