## kix doctor

Check the Kix installation

Reports where Kix found the Kix runtime (nix, helm, kubectl, sops), checks that its manifest.json lists the programs Kix expects, and checks every file against its SHA-256 in the manifest. Also reports the project's builder and where it was chosen (kix.toml, or the default), the version of Kix the project needs, and the installed versions of Kix. Exits 1 when a check fails.

Usage: kix doctor [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (-v, -vv, etc.)
          
          [env: KIX_VERBOSE]

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output
          
          [env: KIX_QUIET]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (also respects NO_COLOR env per no-color.org spec)

      --flake <FLAKE>
          Flake reference to evaluate clusters from (default: current directory)
          
          [env: KIX_FLAKE]
          [default: .]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

