          Possible values:
          - text
          - json
          - yaml
          - markdown: GitHub-flavored markdown suitable for PR comments
          
          [env: KIX_OUTPUT]

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (-v, -vv, etc.)
          
          [env: KIX_VERBOSE]

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output
          
          [env: KIX_QUIET]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (also respects NO_COLOR env per no-color.org spec)

      --flake <FLAKE>
          Flake reference to evaluate clusters from (default: current directory)
          
          [env: KIX_FLAKE]
          [default: .]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

## kix pin set

Resolve a tag and write it into the pin file

Usage: kix pin set [OPTIONS] <KEY>

Arguments:
  <KEY>
          Pin key read by the cluster definition (`pins.get "<key>"`), or `<namespace>/<instance>` to set an instance's image option directly

Options:
      --option <OPTION>
          Config option path to set for an instance pin (e.g., `server.image`). Defaults to `image`

      --tag <TAG>
          Image tag to resolve and record alongside the digest

      --repository <REPOSITORY>
          Image repository, including the registry host. Required when creating a new pin; defaults to the existing repository when updating

      --digest <DIGEST>
          Record this digest directly instead of querying the registry (for air-gapped environments)

      --no-resolve
          Record the tag without resolving a digest from the registry

      --source-rev <SOURCE_REV>
          Source revision the image was built from, verified by `kix pin check --source-rev`

      --promoted-by <PROMOTED_BY>
          Identity of the promoter (defaults to the CI run or `user@host`)

      --note <NOTE>
          Free-form note stored on the pin entry. Preserved when re-pinning the same image, cleared when switching to a different image unless a new note is provided, or cleared explicitly with `""`

      --init
          Create the pin file if missing, or add a new named pin (not required for `<namespace>/<instance>` pins)

      --force
          Overwrite a pin file that was not generated by `kix pin`

      --pins-file <PINS_FILE>
          Path to the pin file. If omitted, Kix searches the working directory, the flake directory, and the repository for a single `*pins.json` file

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format (text, json, yaml, markdown). Default varies by command

          Possible values:
          - text
          - json
          - yaml
          - markdown: GitHub-flavored markdown suitable for PR comments
          
          [env: KIX_OUTPUT]

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (-v, -vv, etc.)
          
          [env: KIX_VERBOSE]

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output
          
          [env: KIX_QUIET]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (also respects NO_COLOR env per no-color.org spec)

      --flake <FLAKE>
          Flake reference to evaluate clusters from (default: current directory)
          
          [env: KIX_FLAKE]
          [default: .]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

