## kix pin check

Verify that every pin still resolves to its recorded digest

Usage: kix pin check [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --key <KEYS>
          Check only the specified pin key or `<namespace>/<instance>` (repeatable; defaults to all pins)

      --source-rev <SOURCE_REV>
          Require every pin that records a source revision to match this value

      --allow-unresolved
          Warn instead of failing when a pin has no recorded digest

      --offline
          Validate the pin file's structure without contacting any registry

      --pins-file <PINS_FILE>
          Path to the pin file. If omitted, Kix searches the working directory, the flake directory, and the repository for a single `*pins.json` file

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format (text, json, yaml, markdown). Default varies by command

          Possible values:
          - text
          - json
          - yaml
          - markdown: GitHub-flavored markdown suitable for PR comments
          
          [env: KIX_OUTPUT]

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase verbosity (-v, -vv, etc.)
          
          [env: KIX_VERBOSE]

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output
          
          [env: KIX_QUIET]

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (also respects NO_COLOR env per no-color.org spec)

      --flake <FLAKE>
          Flake reference to evaluate clusters from (default: current directory)
          
